{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"\u548c\u66a6\u3068\u897f\u66a6\u306e\u5909\u63db\uff08\u4ee4\u548c\u30fb\u5e73\u6210\u30fb\u662d\u548c\uff09"},"description":"Convert between Gregorian dates and Japanese era dates (\u548c\u66a6: \u662d\u548c Showa, \u5e73\u6210 Heisei, \u4ee4\u548c Reiwa), handling the exact switch days (\u662d\u548c began 1926-12-25, \u5e73\u6210 began 1989-01-08, \u4ee4\u548c began 2019-05-01) and \u5143\u5e74 (first year). Use it when filling Japanese forms, contracts or documents that require \u548c\u66a6, or when reading a \u548c\u66a6 date. Modes: {to:\"wareki\", date:\"YYYY-MM-DD\"}; {to:\"seireki\", era, year, month, day}; {to:\"wareki\", year_only} (lists every era in that year). A \u5e73\u6210 date after 2019-04-30 (e.g. \u5e73\u621031\u5e745\u67081\u65e5) is read as that day and the correct \u4ee4\u548c form is returned with a note; a Showa date from 1989-01-08 on (e.g. \u662d\u548c64\u5e741\u67088\u65e5, Showa 64-01-08), dates that do not exist, and dates before 1926-12-25 return an error.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"date":{"description":"to \u304c wareki \u306e\u6642\u306e\u897f\u66a6\u306e\u65e5\uff08YYYY-MM-DD\uff09","maxLength":10,"type":"string"},"day":{"maximum":31,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"era":{"description":"to \u304c seireki \u306e\u6642\u306e\u5143\u53f7","enum":["showa","heisei","reiwa","\u662d\u548c","\u5e73\u6210","\u4ee4\u548c"],"type":"string"},"month":{"maximum":12,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"to":{"description":"wareki\uff1d\u897f\u66a6\u304b\u3089\u548c\u66a6\u3078\u3001seireki\uff1d\u548c\u66a6\u304b\u3089\u897f\u66a6\u3078","enum":["wareki","seireki"],"type":"string"},"year":{"description":"\u5143\u53f7\u306e\u5e74\uff08\u5143\u5e74\u306f 1\uff09","maximum":99,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"year_only":{"description":"to \u304c wareki \u3067\u30